A record whose session-key packet names a key this machine holds and still fails to decrypt now fails `check` and `unseal`. gpg reports such a packet as `NO_SECKEY`, so one flipped byte made the record read as belonging to another wrap group, and `unseal` restored the rest of the vault without it. A record is skipped only when every `pkdecrypt_failed` code is 17 or the keyring holds none of the keys it names. `unseal` now prints how many records it could not open, and fails when it can open none instead of reporting an empty vault.
